	(text "C2: reduce noise (suggested by operational manufacturer)\nC3: reduce high frequency noise\nC4: bulk capacitor\n\nC3 and C4 are not mandatory, it's a design choice."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 175.26 153.67 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "41a35e99-b65d-42ab-ad90-dbc9949105b2")
	)
	(text "GPIO4 is the output of the SHARP sensor\nand it's used to read the measured value via J1\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 109.22 166.37 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "660837b4-ad22-419a-af23-4d5d11c5119e")
	)
	(text "GPIO5 is the input of the SHARP sensor.\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 97.79 118.11 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "814f57a3-1a0e-4245-b143-d29a8d19376c")
	)
	(text "R4 + R5 are used adapt V of the\noutput of Sharp sensor to 3.3V.\n\nWith both R4 and R5 = 10k:\nVu1.1 = Vsensor * (R5 / (R4+R5)) = VSensor / 2\nthis will reduce the max V = 5V to 2.5V.\n\nThis choise will reuire to adapt firmware to manage 2.5V as max value."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 212.09 185.42 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "836cdf73-acf6-47a8-bae3-733af5152202")
	)
	(text "BOARD HEADER"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 52.07 132.08 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "a73aebee-1c00-49b0-8407-443823dd1e26")
	)
	(text "Q1 works in ON/OFF and it's controlled by GPIO5.\n\nGPIO5 |  Q1 |  J2.3  | Sensor internal LED\n-------------------------------\nLOW   | OFF |        |     OFF \nHIGH  | ON  | to GND |      ON\n\nIn this way GPIO5 at 3.3V can control the LED at 5V.\n\nThis is required, but you can use also a MOSFET if you want.\n\nR2 limits current:\nIr2 = (3V3 - Vbe)/1000 = (3.3 - 0.8)/1000 = 2.5 mA\n\nR3 is used to force B at GND during reset"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 120.65 95.25 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "ce33b929-ba55-4ffc-be91-f6ba83c812c7")
	)
	(text "Requires SHARP GP2Y1014AU0F to be connected via J2 (JST B6B-ZR connector)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 250.19 72.39 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(thickness 0.4)
				(bold yes)
				(color 255 0 255 1)
			)
		)
		(uuid "e18cb9a1-e545-48d5-b13e-7f58e56a4f72")
	)
	(text "ABANDONED PROJECT\nbecause SHARP sensor gives PM2.5 and PM10 as a single value\n\nWe should use this https://www.digikey.it/en/products/detail/piera-systems/IPS-7100-1/22041937\nwithout a real breakout board.\nSo this project has been abandoned"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 71.12 44.45 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 4 4)
				(thickness 0.8)
				(bold yes)
				(color 255 0 0 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "e20368d4-7456-4f7c-b1ee-f16de60ee433")
	)
	(text "This is a inseguitore of V (Vu1.4 = Vu1.3) and help us to control the internal sensor ADC.\nReq = R4 || R5 = 5 k\n\nWe use also:\nR6: limits impulsive currents \nC5: to reduce noise\nTau = R6 * C5 = 1 uS\n\nThis won't remove all noise, but it's a way to reduce it a little bit.\n\nTLV9001IDCK isn't required by Sharp sensor datasheet,\nbut is used to improve ADC interface.\n\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 295.91 176.53 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "ecc85575-2c85-4bae-9abc-d33ea14b6301")
	)
	(text "R1-C1 are used to power the internal SHARP sensor LED.\nC1: store energy and provides current during power-up\nR1: limits charge current\n\nWhen powering up the sensor the current comes from C1,\notherwise when powering down C1 gets the charge from R1.\n\nR1*C1 = 150 * 220 uF = 33 mS\n\nThese two components and values are required by the SHARP sensor datasheet"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 237.49 95.25 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "f68bb00c-6502-4894-91c6-c4d16ca4322c")
	)
